      "completion_tokens": 1158,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical substance with the chemical formula **$H_2O$**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what makes water unique and important:\n\n### 1. Chemical Composition\n*   **Oxygen:** This is the most abundant element in the Earth's crust and is essential for respiration (breathing).\n*   **Hydrogen:** This is the most abundant element in the universe and is highly flammable.\n*   **The Bond:** When these two elements combine, they form a stable molecule. The oxygen atom pulls the shared electrons closer to itself, creating a \"bent\" shape. This makes water a **polar molecule**, meaning it has a positive end and a negative end.\n\n### 2. Physical Properties\nWater behaves differently from most other substances due to its unique structure:\n*   **States of Matter:** While most substances are solids at low temperatures and gases at high temperatures, water is a liquid at room temperature. It is one of the few substances that can exist naturally as a solid (ice), liquid (water), and gas (steam) on Earth.\n*   **Universal Solvent:** Because of its polarity, water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. It is often called the \"universal solvent\" because it can carry nutrients and waste throughout the body and the environment.\n*   **High Surface Tension:** Water molecules stick together very tightly at the surface, which allows small insects to walk on water.\n*   **High Specific Heat:** Water can absorb a lot of heat without getting hot. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps the human body from overheating.\n\n### 3. Importance to Life\nWater is the foundation of life as we know it:\n*   **Biological Medium:** It makes up about 60% of the human body and is the medium in which all chemical reactions in our cells take place.\n*   **Transport:** It moves nutrients and oxygen to cells while removing waste products.\n*   **Temperature Regulation:** Through sweating and panting, water helps organisms cool down.\n\nIn short, water is a simple molecule ($H_2O$) that is chemically polar, exists in all three states of matter, and is the essential fluid required for all known forms of life."
